DCS 1
cast LABYRINTH
# Labyrinth (REALM-CASTS.md): the maze rebuilds each night; thread, chalk and lanterns against it.

who Thread Spinner Ari
voice 6 1.0
step start
if thread -> again
say Every path here forgets you by morning. Thread doesn't. Tie it at the gate and walk.
ask Take a spool? | Yes=take | I know the way=no
step take
set thread
give THREAD_SPOOL 1
say Tie it tight. The Wallwright can move a wall; he can't move a knot.
end
step no
say Everyone knows the way until the walls move.
end
step again
say Spool holding? Good. Knots are the only thing the maze respects.
end

who Wallwright
voice 1 0.8
step start
if bribed -> told
say I rebuild the maze each night. Don't take it personally. The maze does.
ask Could tonight's walls stay? | For a lamp of oil=bribe | No, do your work=no
step bribe
set bribed
say ...One night. The east run stays. Tell no one, especially the Riddler.
end
step no
say Then walk fast. Dusk's coming and so am I.
end
step told
say The east run stayed, didn't it. Don't thank me. Thank the oil.
end

who Lantern Keeper
voice 4 0.9
step start
say Light's the only map that never lies. Oil's a flask a night.
ask Buy? | A lantern=lantern | Oil=oil | No=no
step lantern
say One lantern. It's heavier than it looks and lighter than the dark.
end
step oil
say Three flasks. Don't spill near the hedges; they drink it.
end
step no
say Then mind the dead ends. They're darker.
end

who Lost Cartographer
voice 9 1.1
step start
say Maps! Partial maps, mostly true. False maps, entirely false, very collectible.
ask Which? | A partial map=partial | A false map=false | Which is which?=which
step partial
give MAP_PARTIAL 1
say Half the maze, and the half I remember. Mostly.
end
step false
say Beautifully drawn. Not one true wall. The Collector pays well for them.
end
step which
say If I knew that, I wouldn't be lost. I'd be a cartographer.
end

who Echo Hermit
voice 0 0.7
step start
say (From the dead end, a voice answers only what you say.) ...say... say...
ask Ask the echo? | Where is the exit?=exit | Who are you?=who | Nothing=no
step exit
say ...exit... exit... (The echo comes from the left. It always comes from the left.)
end
step who
say ...you... you... (The echo laughs, or you do.)
end
step no
say ...nothing... nothing...
end

who Gate Riddler
voice 3 0.95
step start
if riddle_done -> open
say A door, a riddle, a toll. I have the first two. You have the third, or you don't.
say What walks the maze at dusk and leaves no thread?
ask Your answer? | The Wallwright=right | A shadow=wrong | A Hornback=wrong
step right
set riddle_done
give RIDDLE_ANSWER 1
say The Wallwright. Yes. He leaves walls instead. The door is yours.
end
step wrong
say No. The door stays. Think on it; the maze will give you time.
end
step open
say The door remembers you. Through.
end

who Strider Tamer Oona
voice 7 1.05
step start
if strider -> again
say The sky-striders nest on the hedge tops. One's taken to you. I can see it from here.
ask Bond with the strider? | Yes=bond | Not yet=no
step bond
set strider
give STRIDER_SADDLE 1
say Hold still. There. She'll carry you over any wall the Wallwright builds. He hates that.
end
step no
say She'll wait on the hedge. Striders are patient. Tamers aren't.
end
step again
say She's circling. Call her from any hedge top.
end

who Statue Gardener
voice 5 0.9
step start
say The hedges grow back by morning. The statues don't. I tend both; one of them thanks me.
ask Help with the hedges? | I'll clip=clip | I'll leave them=no
step clip
set clipped
say Clip the east run low; the Wallwright uses it. Don't tell him I said.
end
step no
say Then don't lean on the statues. They lean back.
end

who Herd Warden Tobi
voice 2 0.85
step start
say Hornbacks. Big, slow, and they hate the chalk. Mark a wall near the herd and they'll put you through it.
ask Advice for the herd? | How do I pass them?=pass | Can I ride one?=ride
step pass
say Walk. Don't run. Don't chalk. Hum, if you can hum low.
end
step ride
say No. Next question.
end

who Trapsmith
voice 10 1.0
step start
say I set them. I unset them. Same price either way, which tells you something about the maze.
ask Service? | Disarm the next trap=disarm | Sell me a trap=sell | No=no
step disarm
say Done. The next one. Not the one after; that's extra.
end
step sell
say A tripwire and a bell. It's a kind bell. Mostly.
end
step no
say Watch your step. That's free.
end

who Twin Doors
voice 8 0.95
step start
say LEFT: I always tell the truth. RIGHT: I always lie. LEFT: One of us leads out. RIGHT: It's me.
ask Which door? | Left=left | Right=right | Ask one question first=question
step left
say (The left door opens on a wall. The right door laughs.)
end
step right
say (The right door opens. The left door says: told you.)
end
step question
say RIGHT: Ask me what the other would say. LEFT: ...that's the trick. It's always the trick.
end

who The Architect's Apprentice
voice 11 0.8
step start
if riddle_done -> tell
say You've walked far for someone with no thread. The Architect would have liked you. He liked anyone who kept walking.
ask Ask about the Architect? | Why did the planet shatter?=locked | Who was he?=who
step who
say The one who drew the maze, the city, the fields, all of it. One mural. Then the Grey Wash.
end
step locked
say Not yet. Answer the Riddler's door first. Some things you have to walk through.
end
step tell
set story
say The planet didn't shatter. He cut it. Ten thousand pieces a realm, so it could never be lost all at once again.
say Every deed is a piece. Every land you hold is a piece he trusted someone to keep. Keep walking.
end
